// Time zones against reference data.
//
// The zones are the TZif files of the IANA time zone database 2026e, in `fixture`. The `o`, `n`,
// `l`, `r`, `s`, and `z` rows come from Python's `zoneinfo` with the same files, the `q` rows from
// the `TZ` handling of glibc, and the `t` rows from V8's built-in ECMAScript Temporal
// (`node --harmony-temporal`). The `e` rows are hand-written from RFC 9557.
// One `q` row has the answer of RFC 8536 for a rule with daylight time all year, where glibc gives
// standard time for the first hours of a year. The `t` rows with `Z` have the answer of the
// specification, the instant, also where V8 ignores the `Z`.
//
// Each row is tab-separated, and a zone is its index in `fixture`:
// - `o`: a zone, Unix seconds, and the offset in seconds, `1` for daylight time, and the
//   abbreviation at that instant.
// - `n`: a zone, Unix seconds, and the next and the previous offset change, or `-` for none.
// - `l`: a zone, a local time as seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00 on the local clock, the number of
//   instants with that local time, the earlier and the later one, `1` if the clock skips the
//   time, and the instant of the skip.
// - `r`: a zone, a local time, a disambiguation (`c` compatible, `e` earlier, `l` later, `r`
//   reject), and the instant or the error.
// - `s`: a zone, days since 1970-01-01, and the first instant of that local day.
// - `z`: a zone, Unix seconds, the nanosecond part, and the text of that instant in the zone.
// - `q`: a POSIX `TZ` rule, Unix seconds, and the offset in seconds and the abbreviation.
// - `t`: a zone, a text, how to read its offset (`u` use, `i` ignore, `p` prefer, `r` reject), a
//   disambiguation, and the text of the value or the error.
// - `e`: a text that `ZonedText.parse` rejects, with the reason and the offset.
